[Audio:low-tone:Low Tone]
Played by #R$A71E, #R$A8B2 and #R$A991.
Sixty-four cycles of a tone.

#AUDIO0(low-tone.wav)(#INCLUDE(LowTone))

[Audio:footstep-sound:Footstep Sound]
Played by #R$A590.
The two pitches of footstep, which alternate as Sabreman walks.

#AUDIO0(footstep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FootstepSound))

[Audio:touching:Touching]
Played by #R$A0AC for each pass of the main loop while a sound object of the
type #N$89 exists. No object of that type is ever created, so the game never
plays this sound.
Fifteen notes, each with one cycle fewer than the one before.

#AUDIO0(touching.wav)(#INCLUDE(Touching))

In the game each note would be played on a separate pass of the main loop, so
the notes would be further apart than they are here.

[Audio:enter-room:Enter Room]
Played by #R$A0C5 for each pass of the main loop while a sound object of the
type #N$8A exists. No object of that type is ever created, so the game never
plays this sound.
Nine notes, each with one cycle fewer than the one before.

#AUDIO0(enter-room.wav)(#INCLUDE(EnterRoom))

In the game each note would be played on a separate pass of the main loop, so
the notes would be further apart than they are here.

[Audio:sword:Sword]
Played by #R$A672 when Sabreman lands after a jump and by #R$E77B when
Sabreman collects an object.
Sixteen clicks, one straight after the other.

#AUDIO0(sword.wav)(#INCLUDE(Sword))

[Audio:contact-sound:Contact Sound]
Played by #R$E2C6 when an object touches Sabreman.
Eight clicks, whose pitch depends on the y position of the object. This is an
example, for an object at the same height as Sabreman starts the game (#N$9F).

#AUDIO0(contact-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ContactSound))

[Audio:weapon-pop:Weapon Pop]
Played by #R$DF42 when a creature is destroyed.
Forty clicks, whose half periods come from a counter that goes down by two
each time. This is an example, as the number of clicks depends on the low byte
of the frame counter (see #R$A107; here it is #N$03).

#AUDIO0(weapon-pop.wav)(#INCLUDE(WeaponPop))

[Audio:door:Door]
Played by #R$DEE2 when a thrown weapon bursts into dust.
Noise made from the bits of the first #N$30 bytes of the ROM.

#AUDIO0(door.wav)(#INCLUDE(Door))

[Audio:bounce:Bounce]
Played by #R$DED7 when a puff of dust is made.
Four cycles of a tone.

#AUDIO0(bounce.wav)(#INCLUDE(Bounce))
